: \nL32: [Input]\nL33:   * cite0†☰ L34:   *     *     * cite1†Home L35:     * Browse\nL36:       * cite2†Titles L37:       * cite3†Agencies L38:     * CFR Updates\nL39:       * cite4†Recent Changes L40:       * cite5†Issue Summaries L41:       * cite6†Corrections L42:     * Finding Aids\nL43:       * cite7†Parallel Table of Authorities L44:       * cite8†Subject Index L45:       * cite9†Agency-prepared Indexes L46:     * Reader Aids\nL47:       * cite10†Reader Aids Home L48:       * cite11†Using the eCFR Point-in-Time System L49:       * cite12†Understanding the eCFR L50:       * cite13†Government Policy and OFR Procedures L51:       * cite14†Developer Resources L52:       * cite15†Recent Site Updates L53:     * My eCFR\nL54:       * cite16†Sign In / Sign Up L55:     * [Input] [Input: Search the eCFR]\nL56: # cite1†eCFR L57: \nL58: ## The Electronic Code of Federal Regulations\nL59: \nL60: ###### Enhanced Content :: FR Reference\nL61: \nL62: Enhanced content is provided to the user to provide additional context.\nL63: \nL64: ###### Enhanced Content :: FR Reference\nL65: # Title 47\nL66: \nL67: This content is from the eCFR and is authoritative but unofficial.\nL68: \nL69: Displaying title 47, up to date as of 9/28/2026. Title 47 was last amended 9/25/2026.\nL70: \nL71: cite0†view historical versions L72: \nL73: A cite17†drafting site is available†drafting.ecfr.gov for use when drafting amendatory language\nL74: \nL75: cite17†switch to drafting site†drafting.ecfr.gov L76: \nL77: New Finding Aids are now available on eCFR.gov. The Parallel Table of Authorities, Subject Index, and Agency-prepared Indexes are now online! cite18†Learn more L78: Navigate by entering citations or phrases (eg: 1 CFR 1.1 49 CFR 172.101 Organization and Purpose 1/1.1 Regulation Y FAR).\nL79: \nL80: Choosing an item from citations and headings will bring you directly to the content. Choosing an item from full text search results will bring you to those results. Pressing enter in the search box will also bring you to search results.\nL81: \nL82: Background and more details are available in the cite19†Search & Navigation guide.\nL83: \nL84: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL85: [Input: Enter a search term or CFR reference (eg. fishing or 1 CFR 1.1)]\nL86: \nL87: [Input: Enter a search term or CFR reference (eg. fishing or 1 CFR 1.1)]\nL88: \nL89:   *   * Table of Contents\nL90:   * Details\nL91:   * Print/PDF\nL92:   * Display Options\nL93:   *   * Timeline\nL94:   * Go to Date\nL95:   * Compare Dates\nL96:   *   * Published Edition\nL97:   *   * Developer Tools\nL98: ###### eCFR Content\nL99: \nL100: The Code of Federal Regulations (CFR) is the official legal print publication containing the codification of the general and permanent rules published in the Federal Register by the departments and agencies of the Federal Government. The Electronic Code of Federal Regulations (eCFR) is a continuously updated online version of the CFR. It is not an official legal edition of the CFR.\nL101: \nL102: cite20†Learn more about the eCFR, its status, and the editorial process.\nL103: ###### Enhanced Content\nL104: \nL105: View table of contents for this page.\nL106: \nL107: ## Subpart X—Access to MDUs\nL108: #### § 76.2000 Exclusive access to multiple dwelling units generally.\nL109: \nL110: (a) Prohibition. No cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall enforce or execute any provision in a contract that grants to it the exclusive right to provide any video programming service (alone or in combination with other services) to a MDU. All such exclusivity clauses are null and void.\nL111: (b) Prohibition of graduated revenue sharing agreements. No cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall enter into or enforce any contract regarding the provision of communications service in a MDU, written or oral, in which it gives the MDU owner compensation on a graduated basis.\nL112: (1) Definition. For purposes of this cite22†paragraph (b) , a “graduated basis” means that the compensation a cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov pays to a MDU owner for each tenant served increases as the total number of tenants served by the cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov in the MDU increases.\nL113: \nL114: (2) Compliance dates —\nL115: (i) Compliance date for new contracts. After April 27, 2022, no cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall enter into any contract regarding the provision of communications service in a MDU, written or oral, in which it gives the MDU owner compensation on a graduated basis.\nL116: (ii) Compliance date for existing contracts. After September 26, 2022, no cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall enforce any contract regarding the provision of communications service in an MDU, written or oral, in existence as of April 27, 2022, in which it gives the MDU owner compensation on a graduated basis.\nL117: (c) Prohibition of exclusive revenue sharing agreements. No cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall enter into or enforce any contract regarding the provision of communications service in a MDU, written or oral, in which it receives the exclusive right to provide the MDU owner compensation in return for access to the MDU and its tenants.\nL118: (1) Compliance date for new contracts. After April 27, 2022, no cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall enter into any contract, written or oral, in which it receives the exclusive right to provide the MDU owner compensation in return for access to the MDU and its tenants.\nL119: (2) Compliance date for existing contracts. After September 26, 2022, no cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall enforce any contract regarding the provision of communications service in a MDU, written or oral, in existence as of April 27, 2022, in which it receives the exclusive right to provide the MDU owner compensation in return for access to the MDU and its tenants.\nL120: (d) Required disclosure of exclusive marketing arrangements. A cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall disclose the existence of any contract regarding the provision of communications service in a MDU, written or oral, in which it receives the exclusive right to market its service to tenants of a MDU.\nL121: \nL122: (1) Such disclosure must:\nL123: (i) Be included on all written marketing material, whether electronic or in print, that is directed at tenants or prospective tenants of the affected MDU;\nL124: (ii) Identify the existence of the contract and include a plain-language description of the arrangement, including that the provider has the right to exclusively market its communications services to tenants in the MDU, that such a right does not mean that the provider is the only entity that can provide such services to tenants in the MDU, and that service from an alternative provider may be available; and\nL125: \nL126: (iii) Be made in a manner that it is clear, conspicuous, and legible.\nL127: \nL128: (2)\nL129: (i) Compliance date for new contracts. After August 22, 2022, a cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall disclose the existence of any contract regarding the provision of communications service in a MDU, written or oral, in which it receives the exclusive right to market its service to tenants of an MDU.\nL130: (ii) Compliance date for existing contracts. After September 26, 2022, a cable operator or other provider of MVPD service subject to cite21†47 U.S.C. 548†www.govinfo.gov shall disclose the existence of any contract regarding the provision of communications service in a MDU, written or oral, in which it receives the exclusive right to market its service to tenants of an MDU.\nL131: (e) Definition.\nL132: For purposes of this rule, MDU shall include a multiple dwelling unit building (such as an apartment building, condominium building or cooperative) and any other centrally managed residential real estate development (such as a gated community, mobile home park, or garden apartment); provided however, that MDU shall not include time share units, academic campuses and dormitories, military bases, hotels, rooming houses, prisons, jails, halfway houses, hospitals, nursing homes or other assisted living facilities.\nL133: [cite23†73 FR 1089†www.federalregister.gov , Jan. 7, 2008, as amended at cite24†87 FR 17194†www.federalregister.gov , Mar. 28, 2022; cite25†87 FR 51269†www.federalregister.gov , Aug. 22, 2022]\nL134: ###### eCFR Content\nL135: \nL136: ## Pages\nL137: \nL138:   * cite1†Home L139:   * cite1†Titles L140:   * cite26†Search L141:   * cite4†Recent Changes L142:   * cite27†Corrections L143: \nL144: ## Reader Aids\nL145: \nL146:   * cite11†Using the eCFR Point-in-Time System L147:   * cite12†Understanding the eCFR L148:   * cite13†Government Policy and OFR Procedures L149:   * cite14†Developer Resources L150:   * cite15†Recent Site Updates L151: ## Information\nL152: \nL153:   * cite28†About This Site L154:   * cite29†Legal Status L155:   * cite30†Privacy L156:   * cite31†Accessibility L157:   * cite32†FOIA L158:   * cite33†No Fear Act†www.archives.gov L159:   * cite34†Continuity Information†www.archives.gov L160: \nL161: ## My eCFR\nL162: \nL163:   * cite35†My Subscriptions L164:   * cite16†Sign In / Sign U